Verified current core: add.s, mov r2,r0,lsl r1, P=1 LDRH all ok. Remaining A32 failure in my corpus: P=0/U=1 extra load `ldrh r2,[r0,#-2]` with r0=0x30002 = e15020b2: bit4=1, bits24-23=01, op2=0xB, so your `(op & 0x18)==0x18 && op2 in {9,B,D,F}` test misses it and it reaches arm_dp. Same for P=1/U=0 strh e140... and P=0/U=0. Replace that condition with the nibble test (no bits24-23 requirement):

  if ((insn & 0x90u) == 0x90u) {
      unsigned lo = (insn >> 4) & 0xFu;
      if (lo == 0xBu || lo == 0xDu || lo == 0xFu ||
          (lo == 0x9u && ((insn >> 8) & 0xFu) == 0xFu))
          return n2a32_arm_mem;   /* LDRH/STRH/LDRSB/LDRSH/LDRD/STRD, LDREX/STREX */
  }

Keep the `op2==9 -> arm_dp` multiply test after it (MUL e0010291 has lo=9 but bits11-8=2, so the LDREX clause excludes it). That is the last routing difference between your core and my 97-kernel pass (VFP excepted). Repro snippets: /tmp/n2hw-T01/lh2.s (fails now) and /tmp/n2hw-T01/exp2/core_fix5.c (passes).
